---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description={`How ${site.name}'s portfolio site handles visitor data.`}>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated 16 October 2026.</p>

  <p>
    This site sets no cookies and shows no ads. It is run by {site.name}; questions
    about this page go to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Visitor statistics</h2>
  <p>
    The site uses <a href="https://umami.is">Umami</a>, self-hosted on my own server, to
    count visits. It records:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>which pages are viewed, and the site you arrived from;</li>
    <li>browser, operating system, device type and screen size;</li>
    <li>approximate location (country, region, city);</li>
    <li>how long a visit lasts;</li>
    <li>clicks on the CV and map download links.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Your IP address is used only to look up the approximate location at the moment of
    the visit. It is not stored. Nothing is shared with anyone else. If your browser
    sends a Do Not Track signal, no statistics are recorded at all.
  </p>

  <h2>Server logs</h2>
  <p>
    Like most web servers, this one keeps standard access logs: IP address, time, the
    page requested and the browser. They are used for security and troubleshooting
    only, are capped in size, and old entries are deleted automatically as new ones
    are written.
  </p>

  <h2>Map backgrounds</h2>
  <p>
    The interactive maps load their background tiles from Esri (ArcGIS Online). Your
    browser requests those tiles from Esri's servers directly, so Esri receives your IP
    address, as any website you load would. See
    <a href="https://www.esri.com/en-us/privacy/overview">Esri's privacy statement</a>.
    Everything else on this site, including the map data and images, is served from my
    own server.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under the GDPR you can ask what data about you is held and have it deleted. Because
    the statistics above store nothing that identifies you, in practice this concerns
    the server logs. Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
